Reference credits
-----------------

The projects below informed the design of AgentCenter. None of their code is
copied into this repository unless an entry says so explicitly, together with
the file it went into and the license notice it carries.

- MBrassey/agtop (MIT) - https://github.com/MBrassey/agtop
  Terminal dashboard for AI coding agents. Consulted as prior art for agent
  detection and for what such a tool shows (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, Problem).

- Mission Center (GPL-3.0) - https://gitlab.com/mission-center-devs/mission-center
  Resources (GPL-3.0) - https://github.com/nokyan/resources
  Desktop resource monitors used as the performance baseline and as a source
  of ideas only (UI layout, helper-process design). GPL-3.0 code is never
  copied into this MIT-licensed project.

- Stacer - https://github.com/oguzhaninan/Stacer
  Measured as part of the same performance baseline; no code used.

Development tools that are not part of AgentCenter
--------------------------------------------------

Ghidra and REA may be used by contributors to find out where closed-source
agents keep their session state (see CONTRIBUTING.md). They are not
dependencies: AgentCenter does not link, bundle or distribute them, and no
decompiled code is part of this repository.
